In those transactions where there is no closed order, you need to display real-time candles on the chart and calculate the percentage at the current price. This is necessary so that you can follow the transaction in real time. It is necessary that the chart reflects the current situation on the market, as here https://www.binance.com/ru/futures/DOGEUSDT

To display real-time candles on the chart, you need to subscribe to the Binance API Websocket and listen for candlestick updates for the desired symbol and interval. You can then update the chart with the new data received from the Websocket.

First, install the `binance-api-node` package using:

```bash
npm install binance-api-node
```

Next, import the Binance package and update the `TradeDetails` component:

```javascript
// Import Binance library
import Binance from 'binance-api-node'

// ...

// In the TradeDetails component
const fetchTrade = () => {
  // ...

  // Close the previous Websocket connection if exists
  if (ws.current) {
    ws.current();
  }

  // Create a Binance client
  const client = Binance()

  // Subscribe to candlestick updates for the desired symbol and interval
  ws.current = client.ws.candles(trade?.data.symbol, chartInterval, (candle) => {
    // Update the chart with the new candle data
    const newCandleData = {
      timestamp: candle.startTime,
      open: parseFloat(candle.open),
      high: parseFloat(candle.high),
      low: parseFloat(candle.low),
      close: parseFloat(candle.close),
      volume: parseFloat(candle.volume),
    };
    setCandleData((prevData) => [...prevData.slice(-1)[0].timestamp !== newCandleData.timestamp ? prevData : prevData.slice(0, -1), newCandleData]);
  });
};

// Use a ref to store the Websocket cleanup function
const ws = useRef(null);

// Add a cleanup function in useEffect to close the Websocket (optional)
useEffect(() => {
  return () => {
    if (ws.current) {
      ws.current();
    }
  };
}, []);

// Call fetchTrade when chartInterval changes
useEffect(() => {
  fetchTrade();
}, [chartInterval]);
```

This will update the chart with real-time candles for the selected symbol and interval. Note that this implementation may not be fully optimized, but it should give you an idea of integrating the WebSocket into your current solution.

To calculate the percentage at the current price, you can listen to the trade updates for the symbol and calculate the percentage based on the last price:

```javascript
const [lastPrice, setLastPrice] = useState(null);

// Subscribe to trade updates for the desired symbol
ws.current = client.ws.trades(trade?.data.symbol, (trade) => {
  setLastPrice(parseFloat(trade.price));
});

// Calculate the percentage based on the last price
const percentage = lastPrice && trade?.data.openPrice ? (((lastPrice / trade.data.openPrice) - 1) * 100).toFixed(2) : null;

// Display the percentage
{percentage && <p>Current Percentage: {percentage}%</p>}
```

