```csharp
public V Get(K key)
{
    if (key == null)
    {
        throw new ArgumentNullException();
    }

    int bucket = GetMatchingOrNextAvailableBucket(key);

    if (Table[bucket] != null && Table[bucket].Key.Equals(key))
    {
        return Table[bucket].Value;
    }
    else
    {
        return default(V); // If no matching key is found, return the default value of the V type (usually null for reference types).
    }
}
```

This implementation follows linear probing by searching for an available or matching bucket one index at a time, wrapping around to the beginning if necessary. It avoids looping through every entry in the array and instead terminates the search when it finds a matching key or an empty bucket.

