First, we need to design our data schema. A Hearts game consists of players, rounds, and tricks. Each player has a hand, which they use to play cards during a round. A round consists of multiple tricks. Each trick is won by the player who played the highest card of the suit led. Here's how our schema could look like:

```javascript
const mongoose = require('mongoose');

const playerSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  name: String,
  hand: [String], // array of card codes (e.g. "H3" for the Three of Hearts)
});

const trickSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  cards: [String], // array of card codes played in the trick
  winner: String, // name of the player who won the trick
});

const roundSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  number: Number,
  tricks: [trickSchema],
});

const gameSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  players: [playerSchema],
  rounds: [roundSchema],
  currentPlayer: String, // name of the player whose turn it is to play
  deck: [String], // array of remaining card codes in the deck
});
```

