There are a couple of things that need to be fixed in your code to make it work as intended:

1. `locationPermissionsState.shouldShowRationale` should be used when you need to show a rationale message explaining why your app needs the location permissions. However, it is not responsible for leading users to the settings screen.

2. To make the app go to the settings screen, you should check if any of the permissions are denied permanently. If so, you can use an Intent to open the app settings.

Here's an updated code snippet that demonstrates how to achieve this:

```kotlin
