1. Enable "USB debugging" on the Android device: Go to Settings > Developer Options and enable USB debugging.

2. Install ADB on the Windows machine: Download the Android SDK Platform-tools and extract the contents to a folder. Add the folder to your system environment variables under PATH.

3. Connect the Android device to the Windows machine via a USB cable. Install any required drivers for your device.

4. Install 'SharpAdbClient' NuGet package to your C# project: In Visual Studio, go to Tools > NuGet Package Manager > Manage NuGet Packages for Solution. Search for 'SharpAdbClient' and install it to your project.

