To add inertia to character movement in Unity using C#, you can use the Rigidbody component along with the AddForce method. Here's how you can do it:

1. First, add a Rigidbody component to your character GameObject in the Unity Editor by selecting your character, clicking on the "Add Component" button in the Inspector panel, and searching for Rigidbody.

2. Disable gravity for the Rigidbody component (if you don't want your character to be affected by gravity), by unchecking the "Use Gravity" checkbox in the Inspector panel.

3. Create a new C# script named "CharacterControllerWithInertia" by navigating to Assets > Create > C# Script. Double-click the script file in the Project panel to open it in your script editor.

4. Replace the default code with the following script:

```csharp
using System.Collections;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;

public class CharacterControllerWithInertia : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float moveSpeed = 10f;
    public float inertia = 0.9f;
    private Rigidbody rb;

    void Start()
    {
        rb = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
    }

    void FixedUpdate()
    {
        float horizontal = Input.GetAxis("Horizontal");
        float vertical = Input.GetAxis("Vertical");

        Vector3 moveDirection = new Vector3(horizontal, 0, vertical);

        // Add force to your character in the desired direction
        rb.AddForce(moveDirection * moveSpeed);

        // Apply inertia by reducing the velocity over time
        rb.velocity = rb.velocity * inertia;
    }
}
```

5. Adjust the "moveSpeed" and "inertia" public variables as needed to influence the character's movement.

6. Save the script and return to Unity. Attach the "CharacterControllerWithInertia" script to the character GameObject by dragging and dropping it into the Inspector panel or by clicking "Add Component" and searching for your script.

7. Test your character movement in the Unity Editor by clicking the Play button. Your character should now move with inertia.

Remember, for the script to work, your character GameObject must have a Collider component (such as BoxCollider or SphereCollider) and a Rigidbody component.

