2. Sort the given nums array and set ans variable to 0 and j variable to 0.
3. Initialize a variable sum to 0.
4. Iterate through nums from i to the length of nums.
    a. Subtract nums[i] from nums[i - 1] and multiply it by (i - j), then add the result to sum.
    b. Run a loop until sum > k and j <= i in which decrement sum by nums[i] - nums[j] and increment j by 1.
    c. Update ans as maximum(ans, i - j + 1).
5. Return ans.

Here's the updated implementation of the `maxFrequency` method using the altered approach:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;

class Solution {
    public int maxFrequency(int[] nums, int k) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        int ans = 0;
        int j = 0;
        long sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            sum += (long) (nums[i] - nums[i - 1]) * (i - j);
            while (sum > k) {
                sum -= nums[i] - nums[j];
                j++;
            }
            ans = Math.max(ans, i - j + 1);
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
